{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Confirmed RCA: GitHub re-evaluates job-level if conditions during workflow cancellation. Commit 6f4123678c introduced leading always() functions on all seven full-route predicates; those conditions remain true when a run is canceled, so superseded matrix and reusable jobs continue until natural completion. GitHub docs commit 81ade08c workflow-cancellation.md lines 18-22 states this mechanism. Live run pair 31834162663 to 31834896849 showed 1510 seconds of successor admission delay and 1785 runner-seconds consumed after replacement creation, while pre-change controls canceled in 25-104 seconds. This violates the same-change cancel-in-progress contract tracked by smoky-flare-slug. Phase 2 proof: the strengthened workflow-contract test was collected and observed RED at the missing !cancelled() assertion before the fix, GREEN after the held-out fixer replaced only the seven leading status functions, and RED again when one always() defect was seeded. YAML, actionlint over all workflows, lint, typecheck, 8 focused routing tests, and 67 broader workflow-policy tests pass."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786743916840839001,"uuid":"c13d4510-a456-4ccd-8549-6ede15260678"}